percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Working with a system with two cameras (#1705) i noticed that the camera settings requests using (`Camera::set_setting_async`) are  always sent to the first camera, regardless the real camera target.\r\n\r\nThe problem resides in the  `MAVLinkParameters` class that in the` MAVLinkParameters::do_work` function use predefined constants depending on the `work->defined` value has target components.\r\n\r\nI want to try to add a more generic way to set the component target in  the MAVLinkParameters class.  \r\n\r\nMy question is: It's better to (1) add a component id argument (with a default value) to already existent functions like `SystemImpl::set_param_async`, or is better to (2) add a new whole set of functions that will accept also a component id?\r\n\r\n", "closed_by": {"login": "persuader72", "id": 1241624, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDE2MjQ=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1241624?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72", "html_url": "https://github.com/persuader72", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/persuader72/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1728/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1728/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null}, "comments": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/1086966636", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1728#issuecomment-1086966636", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1728", "id": 1086966636, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s5Aycts", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2022-04-03T22:57:18Z", "updated_at": "2022-04-03T22:57:18Z", "body": "Ah yes, that sounds like a correct assessment.\r\n\r\nMmm, overloading with default arguments or add more functions? :thinking: I would probably use these functions:\r\nhttps://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/4dcee2b14945a80276f1b30abd99088ed7009d9f/src/mavsdk/core/system_impl.h#L169-L172\r\nAnd then add the overload 